From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:18:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usage: Tuned for you says why an agent has no card, not "too
 few calls" (#5627)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The advice was worked out of claude's and codex's calls only, the two
names carried three times in the gui (tuneOf, tuneCallsSince, adviseOf),
so an agent past them was invisible to tune, and its blank pane said
"Not enough calls in this range to tune on" — not why: Qoder's calls
were plenty (jackyfan01), they just never reached tune, and an agent
with no setting of tune's has no card for them to earn.

The names come from agent.TuneAgents now, the one list beside the places
tuneWhere reads settings from (TestTuneAgentsHavePlaces keeps the two
from drifting). The answer names the rest: Others, the agents of the
range with no setting of tune's — sessions.TouchedSince, the sessions
page's listing, which reaches further than the calls pipeline does
(Qoder's files are nowhere in callSources) — and Unread, the agents with
a setting whose files magpie may not read here. The pane says so, and
"Not enough calls" stays for a range that really is quiet.

Verified: TestTuneTellsWhyAnAgentIsBlank and TestTuneAgentsHavePlaces
(RED before, GREEN after; the answer names qoder-cn over /api/tune);
context-tune-blanks.test.cjs (RED before, GREEN after, Chromium, en+zh);
context-tune.test.cjs 284/284, context-tune-shapes.test.cjs 20/20,
internal/sessions green; TestCoreScriptBudget paid for by comment cuts
in context.js; go vet, builds (darwin, GOOS=linux, GOOS=windows).

